From 40dac444b4ad925b18a6ebd642622d9df4f0ccdc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 06:52:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] fix(#94): ExecutableProperty.confidence and
 .source_lenses are deleted; old pins files still load
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The defect, verbatim from the issue: "a computed field no reader reads is invisible". `confidence` was a
hand-set number (0.2 to 0.95) at about thirty construction sites and `source_lenses` a provenance list; the
property's own `property_identity` states both are DELIBERATELY EXCLUDED from identity, nothing ranked,
filtered or printed by either, and pins.json persisted them.

Why a consumer is the wrong answer: printing either would present a made-up number as evidence. They are
deleted with their producers (oracle_light's constructions, converge's five, `_skip`'s parameter), and
`needs_oracle` is the provenance that stays. Deleting a persisted field must not strand an existing store:
`pins.load` takes only the keys in `_FIELDS`, so a pins.json an older Detective wrote (both keys present)
loads unchanged and the next `save` drops them; a test writes such a file and proves both. Positional
constructions in test_writer_native passed `confidence` as the sixth argument and would now have fed
`needs_oracle`; they are fixed. The stale golden of `_witness_property`, which pinned a repr containing
both fields, is removed (its converge was CUT by the machine load on the first and second attempt and wrote
a fresh golden that is not committed): the integrator regenerates it at re-pin.

Not closed: TargetBinding.receiver_params (1 OPEN). `_witness_property` has no committed golden until
re-pinned; final converge line "CUT — aggregate deadline exhausted during minimization".

OPEN 3 -> 1. 941 tests across the oracle_light, pins, writer, converge and guard files pass under 3.14 and
3.12 apart from the unrelated `bound` entry; ruff clean under pinned 0.16.7.
